<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <section id="hryvinskyi_activity_log" translate="label" sortOrder="90" showInDefault="1">
            <label>Activity Log</label>
            <tab>hryvinskyi</tab>
            <resource>Hryvinskyi_ActivityLog::config</resource>
            <group id="general" translate="label" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1">
                <label>General</label>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Record Activity</label>
                    <comment>When off, no channel writes to the journal; what is already recorded stays readable.</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="security" translate="label" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1">
                <label>Secrets</label>
                <field id="secret_fields" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Secret Field Names</label>
                    <comment>A value is masked before it is stored when its field name contains one of these words; case is ignored and hyphens and spaces count as underscores, so X-Api-Key matches api_key. Applies to every channel. Names containing password, token, secret, authorization, cookie, api_key, apikey or private_key, and values of encrypted settings, are always masked.</comment>
                    <frontend_model>Hryvinskyi\ActivityLog\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\SecretFieldList</frontend_model>
                    <backend_model>Hryvinskyi\ActivityLog\Model\Config\Backend\SecretFieldList</backend_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="retention" translate="label" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1">
                <label>Retention</label>
                <field id="orphan_days" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1">
                    <label>Keep Activity of Removed Channels (days)</label>
                    <comment>Each channel sets its own retention in its module's settings. This applies to activity whose channel module is no longer installed.</comment>
                    <validate>required-entry validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
